The indicator: plot the rule, not the verdict
The natural way to display a classifier is an arrow on every bar where it fires. For a shapelet that is the wrong choice, for a reason specific to how the threshold is chosen. The information gain split cuts the distance distribution wherever entropy drops the most, which gives it no reason to land in a rare tail, and usually it does not: on gold H1 the best pre-DOWN shape sits below its threshold on 69 percent of scanned bars. That is not a signal, it is wallpaper, about a hundred arrows on a 150 bar screen.
